<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  profiletool's OWN HDR Profile fixture — a CONFORMING member of the HDR Profile
  sub-class of ICC.1 clause 8.10.

  Why this exists. Every fixture copied from iccDEV:Testing/HDR/ carries the
  redTRCTag/greenTRCTag/blueTRCTag trio, and 8.10.1 says those "shall not be
  present" in an HDR Profile. icGetHdrProfileInfo() therefore classifies all of
  them as icHdrProfileHdrContent ("carries HDR content, not a member"), which
  makes PAWG emit H1 as N/A and — by design — suppress H2..H8 entirely, since
  those questions have no subject for a non-member. So none of the upstream
  fixtures can exercise the HDR section past its first item.

  This profile is the happy path. It satisfies every membership condition:

    RGB data colour space, Display class     (8.10.1 class sentence)
    ProfileVersion 4.50                      (8.10.1 version sentence)
    cicpTag, TransferCharacteristics = 16    (8.10.1, PQ is one of 8/16/18)
    NO redTRCTag/greenTRCTag/blueTRCTag      (8.10.1 tag prohibition)

  Deliberately a HAPPY PATH, not a torture test. The upstream fixtures already
  cover the deformities (HdrInvalidTransfer, HdrMissingBToA0, HagcInvalidXOrder);
  what was missing was a profile that simply IS an HDR Profile, so the H2..H8
  items can be seen at all. It is ours to mutate for new deformity cases without
  touching anything copied from upstream.

  Two values are set so they AGREE, which is the point of a happy path:
    - HAGC HDRReferenceWhite = 203.0 and metadata CRWL = 203.0. H7 asks whether
      those two carriers of the same quantity disagree; here they must not.
      (HagcDisplay.icc uses 300.0 with no CRWL, so it cannot answer H7 either.)
    - ColourPrimaries = 9 (BT.2020) matches the colorant columns below, which are
      the BT.2020 primaries chromatically adapted to D50 — the same values the
      upstream HagcDisplay fixture uses.

  Because ColourPrimaries is 9 rather than 2, the matrix column tags are not
  required by 8.10.1 — but they are present anyway: they are a REQUIRED tag of a
  matrix-based display profile independently of clause 8.10, and 8.10.6 requires
  an RGB HDR Profile to be three-component matrix-based.

  REGISTRY CAVEAT (inherited): the ICC dictType Metadata Registry that defines
  the CRWL/DERH/DRWL/DCV/MDCV entry names and value syntax is unpublished, so
  those keys are reconstructions — see the ASSUMED markers in
  IccProfLib/IccHdrProfile.cpp. If the registry contradicts them, this fixture
  changes with the parser.

  Generated through the iccxml WASM path (xmlToIcc), not by hand.
-->
<IccProfile>
  <Header>
    <PreferredCMMType>ICCD</PreferredCMMType>
    <ProfileVersion>4.50</ProfileVersion>
    <ProfileDeviceClass>mntr</ProfileDeviceClass>
    <DataColourSpace>RGB </DataColourSpace>
    <PCS>XYZ </PCS>
    <CreationDateTime>2026-09-10T00:00:00</CreationDateTime>
    <ProfileFlags EmbeddedInFile="true" UseWithEmbeddedDataOnly="true"/>
    <DeviceAttributes ReflectiveOrTransparency="reflective" GlossyOrMatte="glossy" MediaPolarity="positive" MediaColour="colour"/>
    <RenderingIntent>Relative Colorimetric</RenderingIntent>
    <PCSIlluminant>
      <XYZNumber X="0.964202880859" Y="1.000000000000" Z="0.824905395508"/>
    </PCSIlluminant>
    <ProfileCreator>ICCD</ProfileCreator>
  </Header>
  <Tags>
    <!-- BT.2020 primaries, chromatically adapted to D50. -->
    <redColorantTag> <XYZArrayType>
      <XYZNumber X="0.636962890625" Y="0.262695312500" Z="0.000000000000"/>
    </XYZArrayType> </redColorantTag>

    <greenColorantTag> <XYZArrayType>
      <XYZNumber X="0.144622802734" Y="0.677978515625" Z="0.028076171875"/>
    </XYZArrayType> </greenColorantTag>

    <blueColorantTag> <XYZArrayType>
      <XYZNumber X="0.168869018555" Y="0.059326171875" Z="1.060989379883"/>
    </XYZArrayType> </blueColorantTag>

    <!-- No redTRCTag/greenTRCTag/blueTRCTag: 8.10.1 prohibits them, and their
         absence is what distinguishes this fixture from every upstream one.
         The transfer function is carried by the cicpTag instead. -->

    <mediaWhitePointTag> <XYZArrayType>
      <XYZNumber X="0.964202880859" Y="1.000000000000" Z="0.824905395508"/>
    </XYZArrayType> </mediaWhitePointTag>

    <cicpTag> <cicpType>
      <cicpFields ColorPrimaries="9" TransferCharacteristics="16" MatrixCoefficients="0" VideoFullRangeFlag="1"/>
    </cicpType> </cicpTag>

    <!-- 8.10.6 requires an AToB0Tag in EVERY RGB HDR Profile, whatever the
         profile class, as the fallback path for a consumer that implements no
         HDR processing at all; 8.10.3 c) requires it to be PAIRED with a
         BToA0Tag, which is the defect HdrMissingBToA0.icc isolates. Identity
         B-curve LUTs, exactly as HdrBakedLut.icc uses: what this fixture proves
         is that the pair is present and complete, not what it contains. -->
    <AToB0Tag> <lutAtoBType>
      <Channels InputChannels="3" OutputChannels="3"/>
      <BCurves>
        <Curve IdentitySize="2"/>
        <Curve IdentitySize="2"/>
        <Curve IdentitySize="2"/>
      </BCurves>
    </lutAtoBType> </AToB0Tag>

    <BToA0Tag> <lutBtoAType>
      <Channels InputChannels="3" OutputChannels="3"/>
      <BCurves>
        <Curve IdentitySize="2"/>
        <Curve IdentitySize="2"/>
        <Curve IdentitySize="2"/>
      </BCurves>
    </lutBtoAType> </BToA0Tag>

    <!-- A deliberately SIMPLE gain curve compared with HagcDisplay's: one
         alternate, the fixed mixing type 2, PCHIP-derived slopes, and no custom
         chromaticities. The complex layout is already covered upstream; this one
         is here to be readable and to be mutated. HDRReferenceWhite is the
         203.0 default stated explicitly so it can be seen to agree with CRWL. -->
    <headroomAdaptiveGainCurveTag> <headroomAdaptiveGainCurveType>
      <HagcMetadata ApplicationVersion="1" MinApplicationVersion="1"
                    HDRReferenceWhite="203.0000"
                    BaselineHeadroom="2.0000" HeadroomAdaptiveToneMap="true"
                    ChromaticitiesMode="1" CommonComponentMixing="false" CommonCurveParameters="false">
       <AlternateImage Headroom="0.0000" ComponentMixingType="2" PchipSlope="true">
        <ControlPoints>
         <ControlPoint X="0.2500" Y="-0.05000"/>
         <ControlPoint X="0.5000" Y="-0.12000"/>
         <ControlPoint X="0.7500" Y="-0.20000"/>
         <ControlPoint X="1.0000" Y="-0.30000"/>
        </ControlPoints>
       </AlternateImage>
      </HagcMetadata>
    </headroomAdaptiveGainCurveType> </headroomAdaptiveGainCurveTag>

    <!-- HDR Display entries, so H8 has a subject. CRWL matches the HAGC tag's
         HDRReferenceWhite above; DERH is the authoritative display-headroom
         entry under 8.10.5's priority list. -->
    <metaDataTag> <dictType>
      <DictEntry Name="CRWL" Value="203.0"/>
      <DictEntry Name="DERH" Value="2.0"/>
      <DictEntry Name="DRWL" Value="203.0"/>
      <DictEntry Name="DCV" Value="0.708 0.292 0.170 0.797 0.131 0.046 0.3127 0.3290 812.0 0.005"/>
    </dictType> </metaDataTag>

    <profileDescriptionTag> <multiLocalizedUnicodeType>
      <LocalizedText LanguageCountry="enUS"><![CDATA[profiletool conforming HDR Profile (BT.2020 PQ, HAGC)]]></LocalizedText>
    </multiLocalizedUnicodeType> </profileDescriptionTag>

    <copyrightTag> <multiLocalizedUnicodeType>
      <LocalizedText LanguageCountry="enUS"><![CDATA[Copyright (C) 2026 William Li. Generated fixture, no measured data.]]></LocalizedText>
    </multiLocalizedUnicodeType> </copyrightTag>
  </Tags>
</IccProfile>
